{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "JAS",
  "chapter": 1,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "JAS.1.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JAS.1.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "James, a servant of God and of the Lord Jesus Christ, to the twelve tribes which are scattered abroad, greeting.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JAS.1.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JAS.1.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "My brethren, count it all joy when ye fall into divers temptations.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JAS.1.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JAS.1.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Knowing ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "this",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", that the trying of your faith worketh patience.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JAS.1.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JAS.1.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But let patience have ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "her",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " perfect work, that ye may be perfect and entire, wanting nothing.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JAS.1.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JAS.1.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If any of you lacketh wisdom, let him ask of God, who giveth to all ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "men",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " liberally, and upbraideth not; and it shall be given to him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JAS.1.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JAS.1.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But let him ask in faith, nothing wavering. For he that wavereth is like a wave of the sea driven with the wind and tossed.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JAS.1.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JAS.1.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For let not that man think that he shall receive any thing from the Lord.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JAS.1.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JAS.1.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "A man unsettled in his opinions ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " unstable in all his ways.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JAS.1.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JAS.1.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let the brother of low degree rejoice in that he is exalted:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JAS.1.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JAS.1.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But the rich, in that he is made low: because as the flower of the grass he shall pass away.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JAS.1.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JAS.1.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For the sun hath no sooner risen with a burning heat, but it withereth the grass, and its flower falleth, and the grace of the fashion of it perisheth: so also shall the rich man fade away in his ways.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JAS.1.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JAS.1.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Blessed ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the man that endureth temptation: for when he is tried, he shall receive the crown of life, which the Lord hath promised to them that love him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JAS.1.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JAS.1.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let no man say when he is tempted, I am tempted by God: for God cannot be tempted with evil, neither tempteth he any man:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JAS.1.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JAS.1.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But every man is tempted, when he is drawn away by his own lust, and enticed.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JAS.1.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JAS.1.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then when lust hath conceived, it bringeth forth sin: and sin, when it is finished, bringeth forth death.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JAS.1.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JAS.1.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Do not err, my beloved brethren.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JAS.1.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JAS.1.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Every good gift and every perfect gift is from above, and cometh down from the Father of lights, with whom is no variableness, neither shadow of turning.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JAS.1.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JAS.1.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Of his own will he hath begotten us with the word of truth, that we should be a kind of first-fruits of his creatures.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JAS.1.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JAS.1.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Wherefore, my beloved brethren, let every man be swift to hear, slow to speak, slow to wrath:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JAS.1.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JAS.1.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For the wrath of man worketh not the righteousness of God.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JAS.1.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JAS.1.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Wherefore lay apart all filthiness and superfluity of naughtiness, and receive with meekness the ingrafted word, which is able to save your souls.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JAS.1.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JAS.1.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But be ye doers of the word, and not hearers only, deceiving your own selves.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JAS.1.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JAS.1.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For if any is a hearer of the word, and not a doer, he is like a man beholding his natural face in a glass:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JAS.1.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JAS.1.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For he beholdeth himself, and goeth away, and immediately forgetteth what manner of man he was.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JAS.1.25",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JAS.1.25",
      "verse": 25,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But he who looketh into the perfect law of liberty, and continueth ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "in it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", he being not a forgetful hearer, but a doer of the work, this man shall be blessed in his deed.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JAS.1.26",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JAS.1.26",
      "verse": 26,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If any man among you seemeth to be religious, and bridleth not his tongue, but deceiveth his own heart, this man's religion ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " vain.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JAS.1.27",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JAS.1.27",
      "verse": 27,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Pure religion and undefiled before God and the Father is this, To visit the fatherless and widows in their affliction, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to keep himself unspotted from the world.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
